## Control {{controlId}}: Track, Document, and Report Incidents to Designated Officials

**Implementation Status:** {{status}}

This organization tracks, documents, and reports security incidents within the {{tenantName}} M365 GCC High tenant through incident management procedures and regulatory reporting requirements managed by {{variables.systemAdministrator}}.

{{#if securityAlertsActive}}
**Incident Tracking:**
{{securityAlertsCount}} security alerts are tracked through Microsoft Defender incident management:
{{#if alerts}}
{{#each alerts}}
- **{{title}}** — Severity: {{severity}} — Status: {{status}} — Vendor: {{vendor}}
{{/each}}
{{/if}}

Each incident is documented with: incident identifier, detection time, affected systems/users, severity classification, containment actions, root cause, and resolution.
{{else}}
Automated incident tracking has not been confirmed.
{{/if}}

**Reporting Requirements:**
- **Internal Reporting:** Incidents reported to {{variables.systemAdministrator}} and ISSO within severity-based timeframes (Critical: 1 hour, High: 4 hours)
- **DFARS 252.204-7012:** Cyber incidents affecting CUI reported to DoD Cyber Crime Center (DC3) within 72 hours via https://dibnet.dod.mil
- **Evidence Preservation:** Forensic images and malicious software preserved for 90 days per DFARS requirements
- **Subcontractor Notification:** Subcontractors notified of reporting requirements per contract flow-down provisions

**Responsible Party:** {{variables.systemAdministrator}}

**Verification Method:** Examine incident tracking records, internal notification logs, DC3 reporting confirmation (if applicable), and evidence preservation records.

{{#if evidenceArtifacts}}
**Evidence:**
{{#each evidenceArtifacts}}
- {{label}}
{{/each}}
{{else}}
**Evidence:** {{evidenceArtifactUrl}}
{{/if}}
